          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000000",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Nabq National Park"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000003",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Nabq National Park, nestled along the coast between Dahab and Sharm El-Sheikh, is a remarkable blend of desert and marine ecosystems. Declared a conservation area in 1992, it encompasses an area of 600 km² and is renowned for its unique natural features and biodiversity."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000005",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Mangrove Forests: A Coastal Marvel"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Extensive Mangroves:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " One of Nabq’s most distinctive features is its 4 km long mangrove forest."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Unique Adaptation:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Mangroves, a type of amphibious vegetation, thrive in the flat, sandy areas along tropical coasts. Their stalk roots, both submerged and emerging from the water, form a dense network."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Saline Water Filtration:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " These roots have a remarkable ability to filter saline water, with salt being excreted through the leaves."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000011",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ecological Importance:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " The mangrove forests play a crucial role in coastal ecology, providing a habitat for various marine species and helping in shoreline stabilization."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000013",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Flora and Fauna: Rich Biodiversity"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Diverse Plant Life:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Nabq is home to a wide array of plant species, each adapted to the park’s unique environmental conditions."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000019",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Wildlife Habitat:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " The area supports a diverse range of animals, including storks, herons, desert foxes, gazelles, and even hyenas."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Underwater Wonders:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " The waters around Nabq are a haven for marine life, including the rare and elusive Manatee, also known as “Sea Cows” or “Dugongs”. This presence highlights the park’s importance as a marine biodiversity hotspot."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Visitor Experience"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Open Hours:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000021"
              ],
              "text": "Nabq National Park"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " welcomes visitors daily from morning until sunset."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
